      "description": "The Makatote Railway viaduct stands almost 80 metres above the Makatote riverbead on the North Island main trunck line. Building began in 1905 and completed in 1908. NZ's third highest railway viaduct.\n\nRiver is home to brown &amp; rainbow trout.",
